Subject: [PATCH 4/4] lightbulb F6 codex refresh delegate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hermes_cli/auth_codex.py gains _REFRESH_DELEGATE (None by default) and
set_refresh_delegate(fn); the first line of refresh_codex_oauth_pure hands the
refresh to the delegate when one is set (spec 13 §4.3, §5.5). Both refresh
paths end there: _refresh_codex_auth_tokens and credential_pool's
_post_tokens_refresh (resolved by name through hermes_cli.auth). Inert when
unset.

Error contract (read at the pin): failures are hermes_cli.auth_constants.
AuthError built with _codex_err(message, code, relogin=...), as
_codex_refresh_failure_error does. The pool quarantines only when
relogin_required is True AND code is a terminal code (invalid_grant,
invalid_token, refresh_token_reused, codex_refresh_failed,
codex_auth_missing_refresh_token). So the bridge delegate raises
_codex_err(msg, "invalid_grant", relogin=True) for a dead grant (broker 410)
and any code with relogin=False for busy/5xx/timeout.

_read_codex_tokens accepts the placeholder refresh token
"lightbulb-brokered" (it only checks non-empty).

With a delegate set: _recover_codex_tokens_from_cli is off, so a Codex CLI
login on the box can never put a real refresh token into the VM's
auth.json; the delegate's return is validated (non-empty string tokens, else
AuthError lightbulb_refresh_invalid, relogin False); and waiters holding the
same stale access token share one broker refresh (the placeholder refresh
token never rotates, so the peer-rotation adopt check cannot fire).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
